    "qualifierLines": [
      "{**28 NY3d at 112} OPINION OF THE COURT",
      "Supreme Court denied defendant's motion to dismiss the DNA indictment as defective and in violation of defendant's right to a speedy trial, and upheld the amendment of the indictment. The court held that the prosecution was not time-barred on speedy trial grounds because investigators had exercised \"reasonable diligence\" in attempting to locate defendant. Defendant then pleaded guilty to each count in the amended indictment. As a condition of the plea, he also executed a written waiver of his right to appeal. Supreme Court sentenced defendant{**28 NY3d at 115} as promised to a 15-year prison term on each count (to run concurrently), with five years' postrelease supervision."
    ],
